Relevant columns and their potential usage
- `date`: extract the calendar year ( 2022 , 2023 ) for the YoY comparison  
- `item_description`: the individual liquor product whose sales we are measuring  
- `sale_dollars`: revenue used to calculate yearly totals and growth rates  

Typical conditions that will be useful
- `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)` – restrict rows to the two years we are comparing  
- `sale_dollars IS NOT NULL` – safeguard against nulls  
- (optional) `sale_dollars > 0` when you want only positive–revenue rows  
- (optional) `SUM(sale_dollars_2022) > 0` to avoid divide‑by‑zero when computing growth  

Below are ten progressively more sophisticated BigQuery SQL queries (each different, each limited to 20 rows where practical).  
Replace back‑ticked identifiers only if you copy–paste somewhere else; they already point to the correct public dataset.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a handful of recent rows to see raw data
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
ORDER BY date DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Distinct calendar years present in the table
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Total sales dollars per year (all items)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS yr,
  SUM(sale_dollars) AS total_sales
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE sale_dollars IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Sample of unique item descriptions that were sold in 2023
SELECT DISTINCT item_description
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2023
ORDER BY item_description
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Year‑to‑date sales for one specific item (“BULLEIT” as
-- loose string filter) – shows how to zoom in on a product
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS yr,
  SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_dollars
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE LOWER(item_description) LIKE '%bulleit%'
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Sales by item and year, restricted to 2022 or 2023
SELECT
  item_description,
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS yr,
  SUM(sale_dollars) AS sales_dollars
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)
GROUP BY item_description, yr
ORDER BY item_description, yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Pivot the previous result so each item has 2022 and 2023 totals
SELECT
  item_description,
  SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2022 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2022,
  SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2023 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2023
FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)
GROUP BY item_description
HAVING sales_2022 IS NOT NULL OR sales_2023 IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY item_description
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute YoY growth percentage and order descending
SELECT
  item_description,
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100 AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM (
  SELECT
    item_description,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2022 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2022,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2023 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2023
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)
  GROUP BY item_description
)
WHERE sales_2022 > 0        -- avoid divide‑by‑zero and negative bases
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but keep only items whose 2022 sales
-- were at least $1,000, to filter out tiny bases that distort percentages
SELECT
  item_description,
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100 AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM (
  SELECT
    item_description,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2022 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2022,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2023 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2023
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)
  GROUP BY item_description
)
WHERE sales_2022 > 1000
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – Top 5 items with the highest year‑over‑year growth
-- percentage in total sales dollars in 2023 vs 2022.
SELECT
  item_description,
  sales_2022,
  sales_2023,
  ROUND(SAFE_DIVIDE(sales_2023 - sales_2022, sales_2022) * 100, 2) AS yoy_growth_pct
FROM (
  SELECT
    item_description,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2022 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2022,
    SUM(CASE WHEN EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2023 THEN sale_dollars END) AS sales_2023
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`
  WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) IN (2022, 2023)
  GROUP BY item_description
)
WHERE sales_2022 > 0                       -- positive base year
  AND sales_2023 IS NOT NULL               -- had sales in 2023
ORDER BY yoy_growth_pct DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

